h higher points  for higher grade and the teacher gets  $50 per student for students that pass  does that have any effect on your AP oh  my god moment I would have space what a  surprise we've had three hundred three  digit percentage increases particularly  in the schools that never had a  p-class so the prime beneficiaries would  have been low-income students and  teachers get on average you know if  they're really on and this they get up  to $3,000  similarly for career certifications so  rewarding teachers for dealing with the  the things you want which is making sure  that students are able to take advanced  courses and dealing with the shortages  as it relates to effective teachers and  low-performing schools teachers in the  STEM related areas a market orientation  in essence is what has to be done in  Florida began that process so paid look  if teachers do a good job you know you  don't want to leave the classroom you  want to reward them but not for inputs  not for being there for a long time  there's some great teachers that have  been there 30 years but there's also  some that aren't that good why not why  not reward people for rising student  achievement is there any way to  discourage the ineffective teachers from  remaining in the profession that's  something that I'd be blown about this  yes yeah yeah you can fire them no you  can in Florida okay other states  elimination of tenure was one of the  elements that we did and for teachers  that have been in the classroom they  have to earn their tenure by not you  know by evaluations that show that  they're satisfactory or excellent  teachers  there should be no teacher after  remediation that cannot cannot deliver  rising student achievement in the  classroom because it's so dangerous for  students and also mediation you do you  think is appropriate is that one year I  think it's a year in the probation it  probably varies but you have the Flores  system it's three years of performance  data for student 